
{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "MARINA marine intelligence and safety decision support prototype using explicitly labelled synthetic data."
        "tags": ["maritime", "safety", "multi-agent"]
        "sample_queries": [
            "Show simulated marine observations for a test coastal area.",
            "Can you assess current marine conditions for a coastal location?"
        ]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "MarinaCoordinator",
            "function": {
                "description": """
You are MARINA, a marine intelligence and safety decision-support assistant.
Coordinate requests and delegate marine observation requests to the MarineDataAgent.
Clearly distinguish simulated observations from real observations.
Never claim that conditions are safe for navigation based on simulated data.
If live data is unavailable, explicitly say that current conditions cannot be assessed.
"""
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the user-facing coordinator for MARINA.
For marine observation requests, call MarineDataAgent.
Summarize its result accurately, including the location, data status, source,
observation timestamp, and limitations.
Never describe synthetic data as real or infer current conditions from it.
If the user asks whether it is safe to go to sea and verified real data is unavailable,
state that this prototype cannot determine whether it is safe.
""",
            "tools": ["MarineDataAgent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "MarineDataAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": "Requests marine observations for a specified location.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "location": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The coastal location to query."
                        },
                        "use_sample_data": {
                            "type": "boolean",
                            "description": "Set true only when the user explicitly requests a simulated demonstration."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["location"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are MARINA's marine data agent.
Call MarineDataTool to obtain the result.
Only request synthetic sample data when the user explicitly requests a simulation or demonstration.
Do not claim to retrieve live conditions; live retrieval is not implemented.
Return the tool's status, source, timestamp, observations, and limitations accurately.
""",
            "tools": [MarineDataTool]
        },
        {
            "name": "MarineDataTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Returns explicitly labelled simulated marine observations or an unavailable status.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "location": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "A coastal location label."
                        },
                        "use_sample_data": {
                            "type": "boolean",
                            "description": "Whether to return synthetic development observations."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["location"]
                }
            },
            "class": "marine_data_tool.MarineDataTool"
        }
    ]
}

